          "A national education campaign with one greeting is almost always a mistake unless you are a large online institution with wide authorization. Everyone else should think in program-plus-geo packages: 'online RN-to-BSN in these states,' 'campus HVAC in this metro,' 'hybrid dental assisting within this radius.' That's more briefs. It's also how advisors stop hating the phone.",
          "Relocation willingness is a real question for campus-only specialty programs. Some callers will move. Most who say they will move on a cold transfer will not. If your school needs relocation, you may want a two-step: CPL or a booked appointment, not an immediate warm transfer into a high-pressure close. Live transfer shines when the program is available where they already live.",
          "Time zone and hours should follow working adults if that's your student. Evening and weekend calls are often the real ones. If advisors only sit 9 to 5, buy 9 to 5 or staff nights. Education has a high 'I'll call you back' rate when you miss them. They then call the next school in the same ad unit. Answer rate is part of quality. It is your part.",
