          "CPL works for inquiry forms, info-session registrations, and application starts. It's often the better first model for long-cycle degrees. Keep program and geo on the form. A name-and-email 'request info' CPL will look cheap and behave like 2012. You already know how those files die in the CRM.",
          "Warm transfers should include program, modality, geo, and start-window. Live click-to-call needs an IVR that can fail a wrong program. If you cannot IVR the program because you have forty of them, use buckets that map to actual advisor teams, not to a single 'admissions' overflow that then cold-transfers internally. Internal cold transfers after you already paid for a warm one is how you double-handle and still miss starts.",
